External HSL library packages:

  * ea23 from the HSL2002 library (needed for eigenvalue/vector computations
    in the log-conformation.

  * updated versions of MA41 and MA57, where the last now includes scaling
    of the matrix.

  * fakemetis is really part of MA57, but is only needed if metis has not been
    installed.

  * mc75 used for the condition number of a sparse matrix.

  * hsl_mi20, mi24, mi26 for iterative solvers and AMG solvers.

Notes:

  - The MA57 routine requires a link to the MeTiS-4 library. The MeTiS package
    can be obtained from http://glaros.dtc.umn.edu/gkhome/metis/metis/download.
    Adjust Mdefs.mk according to the directions given in the comments.

  - The HSL routines/packages can be obtained free of charge by academics
    for research and teaching purposes. See the website: http://hsl.rl.ac.uk/

  - The obtained packages need be processed to fit the scheme here. The HSL
    packages contain the main file in double precision and a dependencies file
    ddeps.f. In order to avoid multiple symbols in a library if multiple
    packages are used, the dependencies file needs to split into separate
    files, where for example the routines mc21ad.f, mc21bd.f etc are contained
    in one file mc21d.f.



